  "described": {
    "alt_text": "Four small airbrush studies in a grid, three in soft blue and grey and one in pastel rainbow, each of blobby layered shapes.",
    "description": "A square photograph of four airbrush studies on paper arranged two by two. The top left is a tall L shaped blue block with grey shading and a drifting white shape. The top right is a rounded blue block over horizontal bands and small stalk shapes. The bottom left is a pale blue arcade of three arches with grey insides, above bands. The bottom right repeats a similar architecture of blobs in overlapping pink, orange, mint, lilac and yellow with white highlights. All are sprayed softly with no outlines and white gaps between shapes.",
    "impression": "A page of experiments: the same way of building a picture out of overlapping stencil layers tried in cool blue three times and then in full colour once. It reads like a sketchbook spread, and it explains how the bigger airbrush pieces were made. Soft and watery.",
